# PMC — High prefix count peers
# Canvas: pmc | Collection: pmc.peers
# Description: Peers advertising large numbers of prefixes (transit or route-server exposure)

# Prompt: show peers with most prefixes
# Prompt: list high prefix peers
# Prompt: which peers advertise the most routes
# Prompt: show transit peers
# Prompt: peers with large routing tables
# The lines above are paraphrases of ONE question for the NL widget. The pmc adapter
# (tools/iqe/adapters/pmc.py) has no prefix-count branch, and no threshold for "high"
# is defined anywhere, so the query returns every peer's prefix counts, unranked;
# no threshold is invented here.
foreach p in pmc.peers
select p.asn, p.org_name, p.peer_type, p.ipv4_prefix_count, p.ipv6_prefix_count
# Not applied: IQE has no `order by`, so the executor returns every matching row, unsorted and uncapped. Intended presentation, not performed: sort by p.ipv4_prefix_count desc, then p.ipv6_prefix_count desc.
